WEBVTT

NOTE Draft cue timing follows measured scene audio and word count. Review spoken word alignment before publication.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.495
Welcome to Resgrid Academy. In this lesson, we will assign learning and track

00:00:05.495 --> 00:00:10.991
qualifications. Scattered training records make it harder to see incomplete assignments and upcoming

00:00:10.991 --> 00:00:16.486
certification renewals. We will explain the features, the setup decisions, and a practical

00:00:16.486 --> 00:00:18.600
way to check the result.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.530
EMT and Driver/Operator certification types are added with their renewal periods, and an

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:29.860
annual refresher training is assigned to every member. See who is qualified and

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:35.190
whose certifications are expiring before it affects who can respond. The examples in

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:40.520
this series use a fictional department and are teaching scenarios, not default settings.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:46.367
Trainings. Training assignments with materials and optional quizzes. Create a training and assign

00:00:46.367 --> 00:00:51.615
it to the members or groups who need it. Availability also depends on

00:00:51.615 --> 00:00:54.440
Training. Check access in the target department.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:01.824
Certification Types. The certifications and qualifications you track. Add each certification type with

00:01:01.824 --> 00:01:03.390
its renewal period.

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:10.907
Certification Dashboard. Who holds which certifications and what is expiring. Record members' current

00:01:10.907 --> 00:01:14.100
certifications, then review what expires soon.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:20.468
New Training. Create a training, with an optional quiz. List the certifications your

00:01:20.468 --> 00:01:26.235
department tracks and their renewal periods. Availability also depends on Training. Check access

00:01:26.235 --> 00:01:28.010
in the target department.

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:35.157
Certification Settings. What happens when a certification expires, grace periods and reminders. List

00:01:35.157 --> 00:01:39.690
the certifications your department tracks and their renewal periods.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:46.961
My Certifications. Your own certification records. List the certifications your department tracks and

00:01:46.961 --> 00:01:48.500
their renewal periods.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:54.998
For the training scenario, work in this order. Step 1. Create certification types

00:01:54.998 --> 00:02:00.897
with their renewal periods. Step 2. Record current member certifications and review expiry

00:02:00.897 --> 00:02:06.795
settings. Step 3. Create a training with materials and an optional quiz, then

00:02:06.795 --> 00:02:08.610
assign the intended audience.

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:15.408
Now verify the result. Check a sample member completion and certification expiry. Review

00:02:15.408 --> 00:02:21.605
reminders, grace periods, and any configured enforcement effects. A common problem to watch

00:02:21.605 --> 00:02:27.803
for: A completed training, a personnel role, and a current certification represent different

00:02:27.803 --> 00:02:31.140
facts. Track each through its owning feature.

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:36.584
Your practice task is simple. Assign a refresher to the demo group and

00:02:36.584 --> 00:02:41.429
complete it as a member. Review overdue learning and certifications approaching renewal. Record

00:02:41.429 --> 00:02:46.273
the result, who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed. Use

00:02:46.273 --> 00:02:50.000
the linked feature scripts for the detailed screen recording plan.

